## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app` | Router, layout, authentication provider, generated route table |
| `src/components` | Reusable UI components with isolated CSS modules |
| `src/pages` | Pages generated from the requested page archetypes |
| `src/lib` | API client and validation (platform-independent) |
| `src/hooks` | Reusable React hooks |
| `src/styles` | Design tokens generated from the design system and global base styles |

## Design system

The `{{styleName}}` style, `{{presetLabel}}` colour preset and `{{theme}}` theme are
compiled into `src/styles/tokens.css`. Components consume tokens only; there is no
hard-coded colour or spacing in components. To generate a different palette, change
`design.preset` / `design.theme` in the project specification before planning; the
tokens are generated from it, not hand-edited.

Palette: `{{colorBg}}` background, `{{colorPrimary}}` primary, `{{colorFocus}}` accent.

## What is generated and what is not

This project is assembled deterministically from verified templates. Pages that were not
requested do not exist, and features that have no verified implementation are reported as
unsupported by the assembler instead of being approximated. Business logic (for example
metric calculations) is not invented: the dashboard shows empty states until an API
endpoint is declared.

## Configuration

Set `VITE_API_BASE_URL` to point the client at a backend (default `/api`).
For local development against a backend on another port, set `VITE_API_PROXY`, e.g.
`VITE_API_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8000`.

